      "message": "'The fangs are usually taken as Death's' goes further than the evidence. Of the three translations the note itself cites, only gitapress-shiv-stotra-ratnakar.md takes the fangs as Kāla's ('कालके भयंकर दाँतोंसे मोक्ष दिलानेवाले'). greenmesg-kalabhairava.md ('Whose Large Terrible Fangs Liberate us') and shlokam-kalabhairava.md ('by His fearsome fangs He grants liberation') take them as His own. Nothing in the evidence shows that the Death reading is the usual one. The Hindi ('प्रायः ये दाँत मृत्यु के माने जाते हैं') makes the same over-claim.",
